  "dcterms:title": "ToxTransformer - Conditional Variational Autoencoder over ChemHarmony",
  "dcterms:description": "ToxTransformer is a multitask transformer / conditional variational autoencoder that models molecular biological activity. Its brick outputs (trained model weights under brick/moe, a selfies-property-value tokenizer, and brick/cvae.sqlite) are produced by training on the ChemHarmony harmonized chemical-activity store (biobricks-ai/chemharmony, pinned in .bb/dependencies.txt). ChemHarmony integrates >13 upstream toxicology/bioactivity databases with divergent licenses, so the training data - and any activity records embedded in the outputs - inherit ChemHarmony's most-restrictive terms. The repository's own code is MIT-licensed, but that covers the software, not the underlying data.",
