  "biobricks:reviewed": false,
  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by BioBricks licensing-provenance annotation agent (Claude). toxtransformer has no .bb/source.jsonld; its only data input is ChemHarmony, pinned in .bb/dependencies.txt (dvc.yaml stages preprocess -> train -> build_sqlite all consume cache/preprocess/activities.parquet derived from ChemHarmony). The repo's LICENSE/README declare MIT, but MIT governs only the code and model software, not the redistribution rights of the training data or the activity records baked into brick/cvae.sqlite. ChemHarmony (already annotated at proposed/brick/chemharmony.source.jsonld) integrates >13 databases and is classed restricted / commercial-prohibited because CTDBase forbids commercial use without written permission and ChEMBL is CC BY-SA 3.0 (share-alike). Under the most-restrictive-component rule, a dataset derived from ChemHarmony inherits restricted / prohibited. HUMAN REVIEW: (1) confirm whether trained model weights (brick/moe) are considered a redistributable derivative of the restricted training data or fall outside its scope; (2) brick/cvae.sqlite embeds ChemHarmony activity rows and clearly carries the upstream restrictions; (3) if a commercial deployment is intended, ChemHarmony's CTD (non-commercial) and ChEMBL (share-alike) components must be cleared separately.",
